IMPORT prelude

-- Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 (Western Australia) -- the catastrophic injuries
-- support scheme (CISS): no-fault lifetime treatment, care and support, run by the Insurance Commission of Western Australia.
--
-- SEAT: the person catastrophically injured in a motor vehicle accident in Western Australia, or at work ("Am I covered for
-- lifetime care? May I apply, and by when? What will the Commission pay for? Can I challenge its decisions? What does it do
-- to my common-law claim?"). Every exported question is phrased as that person would ask it. What the Act tells the
-- Commission, a hospital, an insurer or the District Court to do is encoded only as what it means for that person: what
-- they must be given, what may be done to them, and by when.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED: s 3(1) (catastrophic injury, motor vehicle injury, workplace injury, participant), s 4 (motor vehicle
-- accident, the rescuer), s 5 (motor vehicle injuries the Act applies to: in WA, from 1 July 2016; not where an owner or
-- driver is liable in negligence; private land; motor sports; terrorism), s 5A (workplace injuries: an established
-- entitlement to workers' compensation; a work injury that is also a covered motor vehicle injury), s 6 (treatment, care
-- and support needs), s 8 (eligibility; damages already awarded for future care), s 9 (applying; residence for workplace
-- injuries), ss 10-13 (acceptance, interim and lifetime participation, applying again), s 14 (suspension while absent from
-- Australia), s 15(3) (notice of the assessment and reasons), s 17 (no legal costs for an assessment), ss 18-19 (what the
-- Commission must pay, and what it need not), ss 24-27 (review and appeal), s 30A(5) (the injured worker's 7-day notice),
-- ss 31, 32 (offences). The common-law side, from the provisions Part 7 of this Act inserted, read in their CURRENT text in
-- their own deposits: Civil Liability Act 2002 s 13A (no damages for care needs while a participant), Motor Vehicle (Third
-- Party Insurance) Act 1943 s 3EA (former interim participants) and s 3FB (no contributory-negligence deduction from
-- catastrophic care damages).
--
-- Edition: the Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 (No. 8 of 2016) as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47531.txt (legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 47531, retrieved 2026-09-07); its compilation
-- table runs to the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 (No. 21 of 2023) Pt 15 Div 3 Subdiv 11, in
-- operation 1 July 2024. Civil Liability Act 2002 s 13A as deposited at
-- ../../../civil-liability-act-2002/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49335.txt; Motor Vehicle (Third Party Insurance) Act 1943
-- ss 3EA, 3FB as deposited at ../../../motor-vehicle-third-party-insurance-act-1943/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47506.txt.
--
-- NUMBERS AND CRITERIA THAT ARE INPUTS. No regulations under this Act are deposited. So the prescribed criteria for a
-- "catastrophic injury" (s 3(1)) and for interim and lifetime participation (s 8(2)), the excluded kinds of need (s 3(1)),
-- the length of interim participation (s 11(1)), any limit on when an application may be made (s 34(2)(a)), the monetary
-- limits and fee caps (ss 18(4)(b), 20), and the period for appealing to the District Court (s 27(5)) are all asked as
-- facts or reported as "set by the regulations". The Commission's guidelines (s 33) are not subsidiary legislation and are
-- not deposited.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 7 (Crown), s 16 (regulations on assessment) beyond its effect, s 20 (fee caps: regulations), s 21 (the
-- Commission's recovery from an interstate insurer: not a question the injured person asks), s 23 (registered providers,
-- beyond s 19(2)(d)), s 28, s 29 (no contracting out: noted), s 30 (hospitals may notify the Commission: noted), s 30A(3),
-- (4) (insurers' duties), ss 33-36 (guidelines, regulations, review), Part 7 beyond the three provisions above (its text
-- in this deposit is the 2016 amending text and is out of date: see NOTES.md), and the Workers Compensation and Injury
-- Management Act 2023 ss 80, 92, 96 and 151 (the employer's liability for expenses ends when the worker joins the CISS:
-- noted only).
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill from the seat of the catastrophically injured person, with
-- the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for
-- public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Motor Vehicle and Workplace Accidents (Catastrophic Injuries) Act 2016 -- the injured person`

§§ `s 4 -- was it a motor vehicle accident`

-- s 4(1): "A motor vehicle accident is an incident caused by or arising out of the use of a motor vehicle." (2): "if, and
-- only if, it results directly from -- (a) the driving of the motor vehicle; or (b) the motor vehicle running out of
-- control; or (c) a collision, or action to avoid a collision, with the motor vehicle (whether the motor vehicle is
-- stationary or moving)." (3): a person injured rendering assistance "at the scene of a motor vehicle accident" -- "the
-- injury is to be taken to have resulted from the accident".
-- Gloss: only the driving, a runaway vehicle, or a collision (or swerve) with a vehicle counts; loading, repairing or
-- falling off a parked vehicle does not, unless it is one of those. Whether it "results directly" is a judgment of the
-- Commission (s 24(a)(i)), asked here as the choice of how it happened. "motor vehicle" is the MVTPI Act's term (s 3(1)).
DECLARE `How it happened` IS ONE OF
    `the driving of a motor vehicle`
    `a motor vehicle running out of control`
    `a collision, or action to avoid one, with a motor vehicle, moving or stationary`
    `helping at the scene of a motor vehicle accident`
    `none of these`

@export Was I injured in a "motor vehicle accident" under the Act (s 4)?
GIVEN `how it happened` IS A `How it happened` @desc How the incident that injured you happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident` IF
    NOT (`how it happened` EQUALS `none of these`)

§§ `s 5 -- does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury`

-- s 5(2): the Act applies to a motor vehicle injury from an accident "that occurs in this State on or after" the day s 5
-- came into operation (1 July 2016, per the compilation table).
-- (3): it "does not apply to a motor vehicle injury if the owner or driver of a motor vehicle has, as a consequence of the
-- driving of that motor vehicle or of that motor vehicle running out of control, incurred liability for negligence in
-- respect of the injury." Gloss: if someone else's negligent driving caused it, the scheme is not for you; your remedy is
-- a common-law claim met by that vehicle's compulsory third party (CTP) insurance. Whether an owner or driver is liable is a
-- court's (or the Commission's, s 24(a)(ii)) judgment: an input. You cannot be liable to yourself, so a driver hurt by
-- their own driving is inside the scheme.
-- (4): on "private land" the Act does not apply unless at least one vehicle involved has WA CTP in force, or is licensed
-- interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme.
-- (5): nor where a vehicle was "taking part in a motor sports event", or for a "terrorist act".
DECLARE `The accident` HAS
    `how it happened`                                                    IS A `How it happened`
    `it happened in Western Australia`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2016`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury`           IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(3)
    `it happened on private land`                                        IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(1), (4)
    `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(4)(a)
    `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(4)(b)
    `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event`                     IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(5)(a)
    `it resulted from a terrorist act`                                   IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 5(5)(b)

@export Does the Act apply to the injury I suffered in a motor vehicle accident (ss 4, 5)?
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `The accident` @desc How, where and when the accident happened, and whether anyone is liable in negligence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` IF
        `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident` (`the accident`'s `how it happened`)
    AND `the accident`'s `it happened in Western Australia`
    AND `the accident`'s `it happened on or after 1 July 2016`
    AND (NOT `the accident`'s `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury`)
    AND (    (NOT `the accident`'s `it happened on private land`)
         OR `the accident`'s `a vehicle involved had WA compulsory third party insurance`
         OR `the accident`'s `a vehicle involved was licensed interstate and under that place's compulsory scheme`)
    AND (NOT `the accident`'s `a vehicle involved was in a motor sports event`)
    AND (NOT `the accident`'s `it resulted from a terrorist act`)

§§ `s 5A -- does the Act apply to my workplace injury`

-- s 3(1): "workplace injury means an injury to a worker in respect of which compensation under the Workers Compensation and
-- Injury Management Act 2023 is payable"; "worker" is that Act's term (asked as a fact).
-- s 5A(1): accidents on or after the day WCIMA s 665 came into operation (1 July 2024, per the compilation table).
-- (2), (3): only if "there is an established entitlement to compensation": the worker "has made a claim" and liability
-- "has been accepted (or is taken to have been accepted) by a licensed insurer or self-insurer ... or has been determined by
-- an arbitrator".
-- (4): "A workplace injury that is also a motor vehicle injury to which this Act applies must be treated as a motor vehicle
-- injury to which this Act applies and not as a workplace injury". Gloss: a work injury on the road goes the motor vehicle
-- way, but only if the Act applies to it as a motor vehicle injury.
DECLARE `The work injury` HAS
    `I am a worker under the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023` IS A BOOLEAN
    `workers' compensation is payable for my injury`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `it happened on or after 1 July 2024`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have claimed workers' compensation for it`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `liability was accepted, taken to be accepted, or decided by an arbitrator` IS A BOOLEAN

@export Does the Act apply to my injury as a workplace injury (s 5A)?
GIVEN `the work injury` IS A `The work injury` @desc Whether you are a worker, and the state of your workers' compensation claim
      `the accident` IS A `The accident` @desc How the incident happened, in case it was also a motor vehicle accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Act apply to my workplace injury` IF
        `the work injury`'s `I am a worker under the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023`
    AND `the work injury`'s `workers' compensation is payable for my injury`
    AND `the work injury`'s `it happened on or after 1 July 2024`
    AND `the work injury`'s `I have claimed workers' compensation for it`
    AND `the work injury`'s `liability was accepted, taken to be accepted, or decided by an arbitrator`
    AND (NOT `Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` `the accident`)

DECLARE `How the Act takes my injury` IS ONE OF
    `as a motor vehicle injury`
    `as a workplace injury`
    `not at all`

@export Does the Act take my injury as a motor vehicle injury, a workplace injury, or not at all (ss 5, 5A(4))?
GIVEN `the accident` IS A `The accident` @desc How, where and when the accident happened
      `the work injury` IS A `The work injury` @desc Your workers' compensation position
GIVETH A `How the Act takes my injury`
DECIDE `How does the Act take my injury` IS
    IF `Does the Act apply to my motor vehicle injury` `the accident`
    THEN `as a motor vehicle injury`
    ELSE IF `Does the Act apply to my workplace injury` `the work injury` `the accident`
         THEN `as a workplace injury`
         ELSE `not at all`

§§ `ss 3(1), 8 -- am I eligible`

-- s 3(1): "catastrophic injury means a motor vehicle injury or workplace injury that satisfies the prescribed criteria for
-- eligibility for participation in the CISS". The criteria are in regulations NOT deposited: an input.
-- s 8(1): eligible if the person "suffers a catastrophic injury" that is a motor vehicle or workplace injury to which the
-- Act applies. (2): participation is interim or lifetime, with criteria for each set by the regulations (an input).
-- (3): NOT eligible if "awarded damages, pursuant to a final judgment entered by a court or a binding settlement, in respect
-- of the future treatment, care and support needs of the person that relate to the injury".
DECLARE `My case` HAS
    `the accident`                                                       IS A `The accident`
    `the work injury`                                                    IS A `The work injury`
    `my injury meets the prescribed criteria for a catastrophic injury`  IS A BOOLEAN   -- regulations, not deposited
    `I meet the prescribed criteria for lifetime participation`          IS A BOOLEAN   -- regulations, not deposited
    `I have been awarded damages for my future care by final judgment or binding settlement` IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 8(3)
    `I reside in Australia`                                              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 9(1A), at the time of applying

@export Am I eligible to be a participant in the catastrophic injuries support scheme (ss 3, 5, 5A, 8)?
GIVEN `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your accident, your workers' compensation position, the prescribed criteria, and any damages already awarded
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I eligible to participate in the CISS` IF
        NOT (`How does the Act take my injury` (`my case`'s `the accident`) (`my case`'s `the work injury`) EQUALS `not at all`)
    AND `my case`'s `my injury meets the prescribed criteria for a catastrophic injury`
    AND (NOT `my case`'s `I have been awarded damages for my future care by final judgment or binding settlement`)

§§ `ss 9, 34(2)(a) -- may I apply, and by when`

-- s 9(1): "An injured person may apply to the Commission to become a participant in the CISS in respect of a motor vehicle
-- injury or workplace injury." (1A): for a workplace injury, only if the person "resides in Australia at the time of the
-- application". (2): in the manner and form the Commission determines. s 3(2): someone with lawful authority may apply
-- on the person's behalf.
-- Gloss: anyone hurt in a motor vehicle accident may apply (the Commission decides eligibility); a worker only if living
-- in Australia and only once the Act applies to the work injury.
@export May I apply to the Insurance Commission to join the scheme (s 9)?
GIVEN `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your accident, your workers' compensation position and where you live
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply to join the CISS` IF
        `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident` (`my case`'s `the accident`'s `how it happened`)
    OR  (    `How does the Act take my injury` (`my case`'s `the accident`) (`my case`'s `the work injury`) EQUALS `as a workplace injury`
         AND `my case`'s `I reside in Australia`)

-- The Act itself sets NO time limit for applying. s 34(2)(a): the regulations may make provision for applications
-- "including restrictions as to when applications can be made". None are deposited, so the answer is that.
DECLARE `The time limit for applying` IS ONE OF
    `none in the Act; any limit is in the regulations, which are not deposited (s 34(2)(a))`

@export By when must I apply to join the scheme (ss 9, 34(2)(a))?
GIVETH A `The time limit for applying`
DECIDE `By when must I apply` IS `none in the Act; any limit is in the regulations, which are not deposited (s 34(2)(a))`

§§ `ss 10-13 -- acceptance, interim and lifetime participation`

-- s 10(2): if the Commission "is satisfied that a person is eligible ... and that an application ... has been duly made, the
-- Commission must accept the person ... as an interim participant or a lifetime participant, according to the person's
-- eligibility". s 12(1): an interim participant "must be accepted as a lifetime participant if the Commission becomes
-- satisfied during the person's interim participation" of eligibility for lifetime participation.
-- The Commission's satisfaction is its judgment: an input. Answered: if you are eligible and it is satisfied.
DECLARE `My participation` IS ONE OF
    `not a participant`
    `an interim participant`
    `a lifetime participant`

@export If I apply, what must the Commission accept me as (ss 10, 12(1))?
GIVEN `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your accident, workers' compensation position and the prescribed criteria
      `the Commission is satisfied I am eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission is satisfied you are eligible
      `my application was duly made` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your application was made in the Commission's manner and form, with the information it requires
GIVETH A `My participation`
DECIDE `What must the Commission accept me as` IS
    IF     `Am I eligible to participate in the CISS` `my case`
       AND `the Commission is satisfied I am eligible`
       AND `my application was duly made`
    THEN IF `my case`'s `I meet the prescribed criteria for lifetime participation`
         THEN `a lifetime participant`
         ELSE `an interim participant`
    ELSE `not a participant`

-- s 11(1): an interim participant remains one "for a period determined in accordance with the regulations"; (2) ceases
-- "when notified" of a decision that they are no longer eligible. s 12(2): a lifetime participant remains one "for life";
-- (3) subject to the same notified decision.
@export Am I still a participant in the scheme (ss 11, 12)?
GIVEN `my participation` IS A `My participation` @desc Whether you were accepted as an interim or lifetime participant
      `my interim period under the regulations has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the period the regulations set for interim participation has run out
      `I have been notified that I am no longer eligible` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has notified you of a decision that you are no longer eligible
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I still a participant` IF
    CONSIDER `my participation`
    WHEN `an interim participant` THEN (NOT `my interim period under the regulations has ended`) AND (NOT `I have been notified that I am no longer eligible`)
    WHEN `a lifetime participant` THEN NOT `I have been notified that I am no longer eligible`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 11(3): ceasing to be an interim participant "does not prevent subsequent acceptance"; s 13: a former interim participant
-- "may apply to the Commission, in accordance with the regulations, to become a participant ... in respect of the same
-- injury".
@export If my interim participation ends, may I apply again for the same injury (ss 11(3), 13)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I apply again after my interim participation ends` IS TRUE

§§ `s 14 -- suspension`

-- s 14(1): for a motor vehicle injury, the Commission "may, if the Commission considers it appropriate", suspend
-- participation "while the person is absent from Australia". (1A): for a workplace injury, participation "is suspended
-- while the person is absent from Australia" -- automatically. (2): the regulations may let the Commission suspend in
-- prescribed circumstances (an input).
@export Is my participation in the scheme suspended (s 14)?
GIVEN `how the Act takes my injury` IS A `How the Act takes my injury` @desc Whether you are in the scheme for a motor vehicle injury or a workplace injury
      `I am absent from Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are now outside Australia
      `the Commission considers it appropriate to suspend me while I am away` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission considers suspension appropriate (motor vehicle injury only)
      `the Commission has suspended me in circumstances the regulations prescribe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commission has suspended you under the regulations
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my participation suspended` IF
        `the Commission has suspended me in circumstances the regulations prescribe`
    OR  (    `I am absent from Australia`
         AND (CONSIDER `how the Act takes my injury`
              WHEN `as a workplace injury` THEN TRUE
              WHEN `as a motor vehicle injury` THEN `the Commission considers it appropriate to suspend me while I am away`
              OTHERWISE FALSE))

§§ `s 6 -- what are my treatment, care and support needs`

-- s 6(1): needs "for or in connection with" (a) medical treatment (including pharmaceuticals); (b) dental treatment; (c)
-- rehabilitation; (d) ambulance transportation; (e) respite care; (f) domestic assistance; (g) attendant care services; (h)
-- aids and appliances; (i) prostheses; (j) education and vocational training; (k) home and transport modification; (l) any
-- other kinds "approved by the Commission". (2): "Despite subsection (1), but subject to subsection (1)(l)", they do not
-- include "excluded treatment, care and support needs" -- kinds prescribed by regulations not deposited (an input).
DECLARE `The kind of need` IS ONE OF
    `medical treatment, including pharmaceuticals`
    `dental treatment`
    `rehabilitation`
    `ambulance transportation`
    `respite care`
    `domestic assistance`
    `attendant care services`
    `aids and appliances`
    `prostheses`
    `education and vocational training`
    `home and transport modification`
    `something else the Commission has approved`
    `something else, not approved by the Commission`

@export Is this one of my "treatment, care and support needs" (s 6)?
GIVEN `the kind of need` IS A `The kind of need` @desc What the need is for
      `it is of a kind the regulations exclude` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations prescribe it as an excluded kind
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is it one of my treatment, care and support needs` IF
    CONSIDER `the kind of need`
    WHEN `something else the Commission has approved` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `something else, not approved by the Commission` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE NOT `it is of a kind the regulations exclude`

§§ `ss 15, 17, 18, 19 -- what the Commission must pay for`

-- s 15(3): "The Commission must notify the participant of the assessment and the reasons for the findings on which it is
-- based."
@export Must I be told the Commission's assessment of my needs, and its reasons (s 15(3))?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I be told my assessment and its reasons` IS TRUE

-- s 17: "The Commission is not liable for legal costs for or in respect of legal services provided to a participant ... in
-- relation to an assessment".
@export Will the Commission pay my lawyer for help with my needs assessment (s 17)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Will the Commission pay my legal costs for my assessment` IS FALSE

-- s 18(1): the Commission "must pay for all necessary and reasonable expenses incurred by or on behalf of a person in
-- relation to the person's assessed treatment, care and support needs while the person is a participant". (2): assessed
-- needs are those the Commission assessed as "necessary and reasonable in the circumstances" and relating to the injury.
-- (3): not liable for (a) excluded needs, (b) needs not assessed, (c) needs the regulations exclude. (4): subject to
-- regulation criteria and monetary limits (not deposited).
-- s 19(2): "not required to make a payment" for (a) anything given "on a gratuitous basis"; (b) anything provided "while the
-- participant is absent from Australia"; (c) for a child, "the ordinary costs of raising a child"; (d) something that must
-- come from a registered provider but did not; (e) anything "provided in contravention of the regulations". (3): "However,
-- the Commission may elect to make a payment" for those "if the Commission considers that such a payment is justified".
-- (5): not required to pay for anything provided "while the person's participation in the CISS is suspended" -- and s 19(3)
-- does not reach (5).
-- s 18(3)(a) bars "excluded" needs outright, even though s 6(2) is "subject to subsection (1)(l)": the encoding follows
-- s 18(3)(a) (see NOTES.md).
DECLARE `The expense` HAS
    `the kind of need`                                                   IS A `The kind of need`
    `it is of a kind the regulations exclude`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Commission assessed it as a necessary and reasonable need related to my injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the expense is necessary and reasonable`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was a participant when it was incurred`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `my participation was suspended at the time`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `it was given to me free`                                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(2)(a)
    `it was given while I was outside Australia`                         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(2)(b)
    `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child`         IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(1), (2)(c)
    `it had to come from a registered provider and did not`              IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(2)(d)
    `it was provided in breach of the regulations`                       IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(2)(e)
    `the regulations exclude it from payment`                            IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 18(3)(c)
    `the Commission elects to pay it anyway`                             IS A BOOLEAN   -- s 19(3)

DECLARE `The answer on payment` IS ONE OF
    `the Commission must pay it`
    `the Commission need not pay it, but has elected to`
    `the Commission need not pay it`

-- The s 18 limbs: incurred while a participant, a need under s 6, not excluded (s 18(3)(a)), assessed (s 18(2), (3)(b)),
-- necessary and reasonable (s 18(1)), and not excluded by the regulations (s 18(3)(c)).
GIVEN `the expense` IS A `The expense`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18 covers the expense` IF
        `the expense`'s `I was a participant when it was incurred`
    AND `Is it one of my treatment, care and support needs` (`the expense`'s `the kind of need`) (`the expense`'s `it is of a kind the regulations exclude`)
    AND (NOT `the expense`'s `it is of a kind the regulations exclude`)
    AND `the expense`'s `the Commission assessed it as a necessary and reasonable need related to my injury`
    AND `the expense`'s `the expense is necessary and reasonable`
    AND (NOT `the expense`'s `the regulations exclude it from payment`)

-- The s 19(2) list.
GIVEN `the expense` IS A `The expense`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19(2) lets the Commission decline it` IF
        `the expense`'s `it was given to me free`
    OR  `the expense`'s `it was given while I was outside Australia`
    OR  `the expense`'s `I am a child and it is an ordinary cost of raising a child`
    OR  `the expense`'s `it had to come from a registered provider and did not`
    OR  `the expense`'s `it was provided in breach of the regulations`

@export Must the Insurance Commission pay this expense for me (ss 6, 18, 19)?
GIVEN `the expense` IS A `The expense` @desc What the expense was for, whether it was assessed, and the circumstances in which it was provided
GIVETH A `The answer on payment`
DECIDE `Must the Commission pay this expense` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 18 covers the expense` `the expense`
            THEN `the Commission need not pay it`
        IF `the expense`'s `my participation was suspended at the time`
            THEN `the Commission need not pay it`
        IF `s 19(2) lets the Commission decline it` `the expense` AND `the expense`'s `the Commission elects to pay it anyway`
            THEN `the Commission need not pay it, but has elected to`
        IF `s 19(2) lets the Commission decline it` `the expense`
            THEN `the Commission need not pay it`
        OTHERWISE `the Commission must pay it`

-- s 18(5): instead of paying as expenses are incurred, the Commission "may pay those expenses by the payment to the
-- participant of an amount to cover those expenses over a fixed period pursuant to an agreement between the Commission
-- and the participant".
@export May the Commission pay me a sum to cover my expenses over a fixed period instead (s 18(5))?
GIVEN `I have agreed this with the Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the Commission have made an agreement for you to pay the expenses yourself from a sum
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I be paid a sum for a fixed period` IF `I have agreed this with the Commission`

§§ `ss 24-27 -- challenging the Commission's decisions`

-- s 24: an "eligibility decision" is one about (i) whether an incident is a motor vehicle accident; (ii) whether the Act
-- applies to the injury; (iii) whether the injury results from the accident or from something else; (iv) whether it is
-- catastrophic; (v) a prescribed matter; or (b) a suspension. s 25: an injured person or participant who "disputes an
-- eligibility decision" may apply to the Commission for review; s 26: a participant may seek review of a "treatment, care
-- and support assessment". A refusal to pay a particular expense is neither, so Part 5 gives no review of it (the
-- regulations may: s 28).
DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `whether the incident was a motor vehicle accident`
    `whether the Act applies to my injury`
    `whether my injury resulted from the accident or from something else`
    `whether my injury is catastrophic`
    `a suspension of my participation`
    `my treatment, care and support assessment`
    `a refusal to pay a particular expense`

@export Can I ask the Commission to review this decision (ss 24, 25, 26)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc Which decision of the Commission you dispute
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I ask the Commission to review the decision` IF
    NOT (`the decision` EQUALS `a refusal to pay a particular expense`)

-- s 27(2): a party "may appeal to the District Court" against a decision in dispute resolution proceedings about (a)
-- whether an incident is a motor vehicle accident or (b) whether the Act applies to the injury. (3), (4): against any other
-- "review decision" -- a decision on review of an eligibility decision -- only "with the leave of the District Court",
-- which "must not" be granted "unless a question of law is involved". A review of an assessment is not a "review
-- decision" (s 27(1)), so s 27 gives no appeal from it. (5): within "the prescribed period" (regulations, not deposited).
DECLARE `My appeal` IS ONE OF
    `an appeal to the District Court as of right`
    `an appeal to the District Court only with its leave, on a question of law`
    `no appeal to the District Court under s 27`

@export After the Commission's review, can I appeal to the District Court (s 27)?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision` @desc Which decision was reviewed
GIVETH A `My appeal`
DECIDE `What appeal do I have to the District Court` IS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `whether the incident was a motor vehicle accident` THEN `an appeal to the District Court as of right`
    WHEN `whether the Act applies to my injury` THEN `an appeal to the District Court as of right`
    WHEN `whether my injury resulted from the accident or from something else` THEN `an appeal to the District Court only with its leave, on a question of law`
    WHEN `whether my injury is catastrophic` THEN `an appeal to the District Court only with its leave, on a question of law`
    WHEN `a suspension of my participation` THEN `an appeal to the District Court only with its leave, on a question of law`
    OTHERWISE `no appeal to the District Court under s 27`

§§ `ss 30A(5), 31, 32 -- what I must do, and the offences`

-- s 30A(5): "A worker who has suffered an injury that is a catastrophic injury must notify the Commission within 7 days
-- after -- (a) an election is made by the worker to retain the right to seek damages ... [WCIMA s 421]; (b) any payment of
-- damages ... is received by the worker, or any claim for damages ... is settled, if the damages include an amount for
-- expenses in relation to future treatment, care and support needs." No penalty is stated in s 30A.
@export As an injured worker, must I notify the Insurance Commission (s 30A(5))?
GIVEN `I am a worker whose injury is catastrophic` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are a worker and your injury is a catastrophic injury
      `I have elected to keep my right to seek damages` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made an election under the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 s 421
      `I have received or settled damages that include future care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received damages, or settled a damages claim, that include an amount for future treatment, care and support
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I notify the Commission` IF
        `I am a worker whose injury is catastrophic`
    AND (`I have elected to keep my right to seek damages` OR `I have received or settled damages that include future care`)

@export How many days do I have to notify the Commission after the election or the damages (s 30A(5))?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many days do I have to notify the Commission` IS 7

-- s 31(1): providing "false or misleading information" in an application or under the Act -- "a fine of $10 000"; s 32(2):
-- obstructing or hindering a Commission officer -- "a fine of $10 000".
@export What is the most I can be fined for giving the Commission false or misleading information (s 31), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for false or misleading information` IS 10000

@export What is the most I can be fined for obstructing a Commission officer (s 32), in dollars?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for obstruction` IS 10000

§ `The scheme and my common-law claim`

§§ `s 5(3), s 5A(4) -- the scheme, or a claim against a negligent driver`

-- Read together: s 5(3) takes out of the scheme any motor vehicle injury for which an owner or driver is liable in
-- negligence; that person's liability is insured by the vehicle's CTP policy (MVTPI Act s 6, encoded in its own baseline).
-- s 5A(4) diverts only a work injury that is a motor vehicle injury "to which this Act applies", so a worker hurt on the
-- road by a negligent driver can still come in as a workplace injury (an inference from the words; see NOTES.md).
DECLARE `Where my care is paid from` IS ONE OF
    `the CISS, as a motor vehicle injury, without proving anyone at fault`
    `the CISS, as a workplace injury`
    `a common-law damages claim against the negligent owner or driver, met by the vehicle's compulsory third party insurance`
    `neither: this Act does not cover my injury`

@export Will my lifetime care be paid by the scheme, or must I claim damages from whoever was at fault (ss 5, 5A, 8)?
GIVEN `my case` IS A `My case` @desc Your accident, workers' compensation position and the prescribed criteria
GIVETH A `Where my care is paid from`
DECIDE `Where is my care paid from` IS
    IF `Am I eligible to participate in the CISS` `my case`
    THEN IF `How does the Act take my injury` (`my case`'s `the accident`) (`my case`'s `the work injury`) EQUALS `as a motor vehicle injury`
         THEN `the CISS, as a motor vehicle injury, without proving anyone at fault`
         ELSE `the CISS, as a workplace injury`
    ELSE IF     `Was I injured in a motor vehicle accident` (`my case`'s `the accident`'s `how it happened`)
            AND `my case`'s `the accident`'s `an owner or driver is liable in negligence for my injury`
         THEN `a common-law damages claim against the negligent owner or driver, met by the vehicle's compulsory third party insurance`
         ELSE `neither: this Act does not cover my injury`

§§ `Civil Liability Act 2002 s 13A, MVTPI Act s 3EA -- damages for care while in the scheme`

-- CLA s 13A(4), (5) (current text, as replaced by WCIMA 2023 s 626): for a participant, "No damages can be awarded ... in
-- respect of any treatment, care and support needs ... that -- (a) have arisen during the period in respect of which the
-- person is a participant in the CISS; or (b) will or may arise in future." (6): an interim participant is assumed to
-- become a lifetime participant. (7), (8) (and MVTPI s 3EA(3), (4) for vehicle injuries): a person who "has ceased to be an
-- interim participant" and "has not become a lifetime participant" gets no damages for needs "that arose during the period
-- in respect of which the person was an interim participant". (3): the needs include gratuitous domestic, nursing and
-- attendance services by household or family. (9): all this whether or not the needs were assessed or paid for.
-- Neither section speaks of a lifetime participant notified that they are no longer eligible (s 12(3)): on the words, no
-- bar applies to them. Needs that arose before acceptance are not barred either. Damages for other loss (pain and
-- suffering, lost earnings) are untouched.
DECLARE `My standing in the scheme` IS ONE OF
    `I am an interim or lifetime participant`
    `I was an interim participant and was not made a lifetime participant`
    `I was a lifetime participant and was notified I am no longer eligible`
    `I have never been a participant`

DECLARE `When the care need arises` IS ONE OF
    `before I became a participant`
    `while I was a participant`
    `after my participation ended`
    `in future`

@export Can a court award me damages for this care need, given the scheme (Civil Liability Act s 13A; MVTPI Act s 3EA)?
GIVEN `my standing` IS A `My standing in the scheme` @desc Whether you are, were, or never were a participant
      `when it arises` IS A `When the care need arises` @desc When the treatment, care or support need arose or will arise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I be awarded damages for this care need` IF
    CONSIDER `my standing`
    WHEN `I am an interim or lifetime participant` THEN `when it arises` EQUALS `before I became a participant`
    WHEN `I was an interim participant and was not made a lifetime participant` THEN NOT (`when it arises` EQUALS `while I was a participant`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `MVTPI Act s 3FB -- my own fault`

-- MVTPI s 3FB(2), (3): damages "in respect of catastrophic injury to a person directly caused by, or by the driving of, a
-- motor vehicle", so far as they relate to treatment, care and support needs: "no deduction is to be made for any
-- contributory negligence of the person". Other heads of damages may still be reduced (by how much is the Law Reform
-- (Contributory Negligence and Tortfeasors' Contribution) Act 1947, not encoded). Same answer as the MVTPI baseline.
@export Can my damages be reduced because I was partly to blame (MVTPI Act s 3FB)?
GIVEN `my injury is catastrophic and was caused by the driving of a motor vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury is catastrophic and directly caused by, or by the driving of, a motor vehicle
      `the damages are for my treatment, care and support needs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether these damages are for care needs, past or future, rather than another head of loss
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my damages be reduced for my own fault` IF
    NOT (`my injury is catastrophic and was caused by the driving of a motor vehicle` AND `the damages are for my treatment, care and support needs`)
